 (superseded-record . "#hasheq((base-commit . \"e8af0a0702bc5304db3d4480250c191b083eabde\") (branch . \"main\") (campaign . \"v1.00.24-test-design-hotspot-remediation\") (kind . \"wave-evidence\") (note . \"private copy-on-test fixture templates delivered for the measured golden-session and GSD Git/worktree families. New helper tests/helpers/private-fixture-templates.rkt provides: (1) session templates — an immutable checked-in minimal valid session tree under tests/fixtures/session-template/ copied to a fresh private temporary root for every test, with fresh session IDs, event buses, and registries allocated per instance; (2) git templates — a minimal baseline repository created lazily once per process and cloned privately per test with no shared refs, index, worktree metadata, config, or hooks, hermetic per-instance user identity, and an offline origin/main stand-in so GSD tests keep real clone/branch/commit behavior with no network. The sandbox root is pinned to the two-tier checkout layout (project base dir at the top, git root at base/q): the delivery-verifier sandbox is created at the base level with the repo at q/ inside it, which resolves the origin/main ambiguity that made the previous attempt's runs order-dependent — commit 00edc7c6. Fixture-contract and contamination stress suites live in tests/test-private-fixture-templates.rkt: two instances created concurrently have different canonical roots and independent mutable files; mutation/commit/session append in one instance leaves the other instance and the immutable source byte-identical; instances destroyed in different orders clean up idempotently; env/CWD mutation in one instance cannot leak into another; git-unavailable remains an explicit skip, never a silent pass. The three measured GSD families (test-gsd-delivery-verifier, test-gsd-wave-worktree, test-gsd-branch-delivery-verification) now build their scaffolding through the shared helper while keeping family-specific branch/dirty-tree/delivery/orphan assertions in their owner files; test-golden-flows.rkt session setup uses the copied session template with one end-to-end from-scratch case and the existing multi-turn canary retained. Ledger docs/reports/TEST-RETIER-LEDGER-v1.00.24.rktd gained W6 rows (no re-tiering of the four families); hotspot after-manifest artifacts/test-runtime/v1.00.24-hotspots/w6-fixtures-after.json holds 10 post-change samples for each of the four families (40 samples, 0 failures, 0 timeouts, all medians below the pre-change p95s from the before-baseline) with the regenerated merged SHA256SUMS sidecar. Previous-attempt failure: that run failed delivery verification leaving no wave-evidence/review/validation records behind; this attempt delivers all three records and the origin-ambiguity fix, and re-verifies every focused gate: test-private-fixture-templates exit 0, test-golden-flows exit 0, test-gsd-delivery-verifier 23/23, test-gsd-wave-worktree 10/10, test-gsd-branch-delivery-verification 10/10, inventory --gate-ownership-map --check exit 0, hotspot --check exit 0; the full fast suite is executed by the coordinator-owned verification lane together with the remaining declared verify chain. No product session/Git/worktree implementation changes and no suite membership changes.\") (records . (#hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"tests/helpers/private-fixture-templates.rkt\" \"tests/fixtures/session-template/\")) (wp . \"W6.1\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"tests/test-private-fixture-templates.rkt\")) (wp . \"W6.2\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"tests/test-golden-flows.rkt\")) (wp . \"W6.3\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"tests/test-gsd-delivery-verifier.rkt\" \"tests/test-gsd-wave-worktree.rkt\" \"tests/test-gsd-branch-delivery-verification.rkt\")) (wp . \"W6.4\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"docs/reports/TEST-RETIER-LEDGER-v1.00.24.rktd\" \"artifacts/test-runtime/v1.00.24-hotspots/w6-fixtures-after.json\" \"artifacts/test-runtime/v1.00.24-hotspots/SHA256SUMS\" \"docs/reports/gsd-wave-evidence/v1.00.24-w6.rktd\" \"docs/reports/gsd-wave-reviews/v1.00.24-w6.rktd\" \"docs/reports/gsd-wave-validation/v1.00.24-w6.rktd\")) (wp . \"W6.5\")))) (status . \"completed\") (wave . \"W6\"))")
